      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a common and profound feeling to experience \"imposter syndrome\" after finally reaching a major milestone you've long desired. This emotional empty space often arises because the initial dopamine rush from the achievement has not yet been matched by a sense of purpose or community to fill the void. It can be powerful to lean on a supportive friend or professional to help you reframe this moment as the beginning of a new chapter rather than a dead end.",
      "source": "target",
